                            corresponding Medieval Libraries of Great Britain index card provides
                            the following context for the rejection: A volume with these contents
                            was described briefly by Bishop Virtue in <title>Proceedings of the
                            Society of Antiquaries of London</title>, 2nd series, XIV (1891-2), 279,
                            as discovered by him at Woolhampton Lodge 1884. It had been found with
                            Reading books at Shinfield near Reading in 1792 (cf. <title>English
                            Historical Review</title> (1888) III. MS. 8451 [now MS 103] has been
                            recently rebound, has no mark of provenance, and may not be the one
                            described by Bishop Virtue.</p></provenance>
